{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"Operator ruling (2026-08-22): the rebar-gerrit-voter-errors alarm fired 5 times in 2 days; investigation proved every incident was a transient, self-healing event handled by designed recovery paths (review timeout -> backfill retry; curl-28 clone stalls under merge-burst load; retryable-gap budgets escalating to the designed fail-closed -1). All affected changes merged with LLM-Review +1; none required operator attention. Ruling: recalibrate the alarm to reduce noise — transient self-healing errors should not page; a SUSTAINED voter failure (the fail-closed gate actually stuck, e.g. expired token, LLM outage, Gerrit down) must still alarm loudly.\n\nCurrent shape (aws describe-alarms, 2026-08-22): metric rebar/host:voter_errors, Sum over period 300s, threshold 0, GreaterThanThreshold, 1 evaluation period, TreatMissingData=notBreaching. I.e. a single marker in any 5-minute window alarms. Terraform source: infra/terraform/monitoring_s4b.tf.\n\nEvidence base (2-day sample, journald + CloudWatch):\n- Transient incidents: 1 isolated marker (double-counted to 2 pre-dedup-fix; companion bug fixes that), clearing within one interval. 5 such incidents in 48h under 4-session heavy load.\n- A sustained failure mode emits markers on EVERY review attempt: the webhook queue + backfill reconciler retry continuously, so an expired token / LLM outage produces a continuous marker stream across consecutive intervals, not an isolated spike.\n- Precedents: mirror-guard 969acad79b4b (sustained-divergence window); 3ff9 ruling (suppress expected-contention noise); monitoring_ws7.tf 2x5-min sustained.\n\nDesign constraints:\n- The discriminator is PERSISTENCE, not magnitude: alarm on markers present across consecutive evaluation periods (e.g. N-of-M datapoints > 0, sized so an isolated self-healing error never fires but a stuck gate fires within ~15 minutes), rather than raising the count threshold (a burst of distinct transient errors is still transient; one error repeating forever is the outage).\n- Keep OK/ALARM actions and the fail-closed rationale in the alarm description; update the description to name the calibration rationale and this ticket.\n- Coordinate with the double-count bug fix (companion ticket, blocks this one): calibrate against deduplicated counts.\n- Terraform-only change (monitoring_s4b.tf + any doc). Landing the .tf through Gerrit does NOT apply it: flag in the close comment whether apply happens via the existing drift/apply workflow or needs the operator; do not run terraform apply against AWS yourself without checking how this repo's terraform changes are applied (read infra/ runbooks + terraform-drift.yml first). If apply requires a human, land the change, comment what remains, and close only if the ticket ACs are met by the landed change per repo convention for infra changes (check how prior monitoring_*.tf changes were handled — e.g. the adb6/58a3/mirror-guard lanes).\n\n## Approach\n\nRecalibrate `aws_cloudwatch_metric_alarm.voter_errors` in `infra/terraform/monitoring_s4b.tf`\nfrom single-period (1x300s, Sum>0) to a sustained N-of-M shape — 3-of-5:\n\n- `period = 300`, `evaluation_periods = 5`, `datapoints_to_alarm = 3`,\n  `threshold = 0`, `comparison_operator = \"GreaterThanThreshold\"`, `statistic = \"Sum\"`,\n  `treat_missing_data = \"notBreaching\"` (all other attributes — namespace/metric,\n  alarm_actions/ok_actions to the shared SNS topic per ticket 9baf, tags — unchanged).\n\nWhy 3-of-5 (grounded in the ruling's \"N-of-M datapoints Sum>0, sized so an isolated\nself-healing error never fires but a stuck gate fires within ~15 minutes\"):\n- Isolated-transient immunity: the evidence base shows transients clear within one\n  interval — 1 breaching period, or 2 when the event straddles a period boundary.\n  datapoints_to_alarm=3 means even a boundary-straddling transient (2 breaching\n  periods) never pages. The house 2-of-2 shape (monitoring_ws7.tf / mirror-guard\n  969acad79b4b) WOULD page on that straddle, so this alarm needs the wider shape.\n- ~15-min sustained detection: a stuck gate (expired token / LLM outage) produces\n  markers on every review attempt — the webhook queue and the backfill reconciler\n  (RECONCILE_INTERVAL_SECONDS=300, src/rebar/review_bot/config.py:279) retry\n  continuously — so under a continuous stream the 3rd breaching period completes at\n  ~15 min and the alarm fires.\n- Why M=5 not N-of-N consecutive: the marker stream (~5-min reconciler cadence, plus\n  the probe's own 5-min offset-delta sampling, OnUnitActiveSec=5min) is NOT\n  phase-aligned with CloudWatch period boundaries, so a genuine sustained outage can\n  yield an occasional zero-marker period (two markers landing in one period, none in\n  the next). N-of-N consecutive would reset its streak on such a gap and could fire\n  late or never; 3-of-5 tolerates up to 2 gap periods (worst-case fire at 25 min,\n  nominal 15) while keeping the isolated-transient immunity above.\n- The probe publishes a datapoint every 5 min including zeros (observability.sh §4),\n  so all M periods have data; notBreaching keeps a probe outage non-paging (fails\n  safe, matching S5).\n- Known inherent limitation (unchanged here): the metric is error-driven — a stuck\n  gate with zero review traffic emits no markers and cannot alarm under any shape;\n  that would need a synthetic health probe (different metric, out of scope).\n- Calibration assumes deduplicated counts: companion bug f829-152a-b415-44a4 (merged,\n  change 2117 / 9b060923451) removed the logger-copy double emission, so Sum now counts\n  real errors 1:1.\n\nAlso rewrite the alarm_description heredoc: keep the fail-closed rationale (ADR-0013),\nadd the sustained-detection calibration rationale and this ticket id ea5d-4932-8554-4544.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `infra/terraform/monitoring_s4b.tf` — the only file changed (evaluation_periods,\n  datapoints_to_alarm, comments, alarm_description). No new resources, no variables,\n  no other .tf files, no probe/emitter changes.\n- Out of scope: running `terraform apply` (applies are MANUAL per\n  infra/runbooks/provision-restore.md §plan-before-apply); any change to the metric\n  pipeline; other alarms' shapes.\n\n## Testing\n\nTest tier for monitoring .tf changes in this repo (per terraform-drift.yml and prior\nmonitoring_*.tf changes, e.g. 24ec1e6d8ac): static validation — CI has no\nalarm-behavior simulation tier, so the two behavioral ACs are covered by the shape\narithmetic above (3rd breaching period at 15 min nominal; isolated marker breaches ≤2 < datapoints_to_alarm=3) plus:\n- Local: `terraform fmt -check -recursive`, `terraform init -backend=false`,\n  `terraform validate` (Terraform 1.10.5, matching CI).\n- CI (Verified gate): repo lint/typecheck/tests as usual; the terraform-drift workflow\n  runs on GitHub PRs + daily cron, not on Gerrit verify — after merge the DAILY drift\n  sweep will FAIL on the non-empty plan until an operator applies; that is the designed\n  committed-but-unapplied signal (workflow header), recorded on the ticket as the\n  application path.\n\n## Application path (recorded per AC)\n\nLanding via Gerrit does NOT apply to AWS. Applies are manual:\ninfra/runbooks/provision-restore.md §\"plan-before-apply on the shared remote backend\"\n(`terraform plan -out plan.tfplan` → review → `terraform apply plan.tfplan`). The daily\nterraform-drift sweep flags the pending apply until the operator runs it. I will not run\nterraform apply myself.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] Alarm no longer fires on an isolated self-healing marker; fires within ~15 min of a sustained marker stream (covered by the 3-of-5 shape arithmetic + static validation — see Testing).\n- [x] Both behaviors covered by whatever test tier monitoring .tf changes get in this repo (terraform fmt/validate locally; drift plan in CI's daily sweep).\n- [x] Description text updated with rationale + ticket reference.\n- [x] Application path (auto vs operator apply) explicitly recorded on the ticket (manual operator apply per provision-restore.md; drift sweep flags until applied)."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787450590626391001,"uuid":"348e2f44-0b6d-4d0d-905b-2e5998a7f175"}